<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_SurgeWeather.xml                 UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M2 build pass

  miasma_kit_spec.md M2: "forced RUT_SurgeWeather during ramp-in (seaward
  exhale: wind sound, thick air)". Forced by RM_GameCondition_GradientSurge's
  own ForcedWeather() override for the whole of the surge's ramp-in Duration
  (see that class's header) - never a scheduled/standing weather like
  RUT_MiasmaWeather, only live while a surge is actively shoving.

  rainRate/snowRate/sandRate all 0, same as RUT_MiasmaWeather.xml - ban #5
  ("no rain") binds every weather this biome can ever roll, not just the
  standing one.

  accuracyMultiplier/moveSpeedMultiplier: INVENTED-BUILD (this pass's own,
  not the kit spec's, which gives no figures for this weather specifically -
  it only names RUT_MiasmaWeather's). Slightly worse than the standing haze
  (0.80 vs 0.85 accuracy, 0.9 vs 1.0 move) - "the sea shoves miles up the
  channels" reads as harder going and harder sighting than the ordinary haze,
  not a new mechanic, just a worse version of the same one.

  windSpeedFactor/windSpeedOffset: the spec's own "wind sound" - a real,
  audible gust during the shove (RUT_MiasmaWeather sets neither, so this is
  the surge's own distinguishing note).

  Overlay: reuses vanilla's own WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze class again
  (RimWorld/WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze.cs, confirmed real, same class
  RUT_MiasmaWeather.xml already reuses this item) rather than commissioning
  new "seaward exhale" art this pass - a documented, zero-new-art
  substitution matching that file's own precedent, not a silently different
  one.

  Sky colours: a darker, greyer cast than RUT_MiasmaWeather's green-gold -
  INVENTED-BUILD, "the sea's own weather" reading as colder/greyer than the
  delta's ordinary breath. All four sets carry nonzero saturation per
  WeatherDef.ConfigErrors.

  ambientSounds intentionally empty, same reasoning/gap as RUT_MiasmaWeather.xml
  (a real SoundDef for "wind sound" is a sound-design content call this pass
  doesn't invent a name for).
-->
<Defs>

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RUT_SurgeWeather</defName>
    <label>the breath-tide</label>
    <description>The sea shoves miles up the channels. Wind carries the smell of open brine ahead of the water itself, and the light goes flat and grey while the tide climbs.</description>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <canOccurAsRandomForcedEvent>false</canOccurAsRandomForcedEvent>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.80</accuracyMultiplier>
    <moveSpeedMultiplier>0.9</moveSpeedMultiplier>
    <windSpeedFactor>1.3</windSpeedFactor>
    <windSpeedOffset>0.4</windSpeedOffset>
    <rainRate>0</rainRate>
    <snowRate>0</snowRate>
    <sandRate>0</sandRate>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_NoxiousHaze</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(0.55,0.56,0.54)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.45,0.46,0.44)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.4,0.42,0.4)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.4</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.5,0.48,0.42)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.4,0.4,0.36)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.34,0.34,0.3)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.4</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.16,0.18,0.2)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.22,0.24,0.26)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.14,0.16,0.18)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.4</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.22,0.24,0.26)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.26,0.28,0.3)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.18,0.2,0.22)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.4</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
